    "setup_id": "05601a00c6bc4954635863826740b7b61d18798ad2f99e32a9fef415a652990f",
    "text": "To determine the number of shirt-and-tie outfits where the shirt and the tie are not the same color, we can follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of shirt-and-tie outfits without any restrictions:**\n   - There are 8 colors.\n   - For each color, there is one shirt and one tie.\n   - Therefore, there are 8 choices for the shirt and 8 choices for the tie.\n   - The total number of unrestricted outfits is \\(8 \\times 8 = 64\\).\n\n2. **Identify the number of outfits where the shirt and the tie are the same color:**\n   - For each color, there is exactly one shirt and one tie.\n   - Thus, there is only 1 outfit where the shirt and the tie are the same color.\n\n3. **Calculate the number of valid outfits (where the shirt and the tie are not the same color):**\n   - Subtract the number of outfits where the shirt and the tie are the same color from the total number of outfits.\n   - This gives \\(64 - 1 = 63\\).\n\nSo, the number of shirt-and-tie outfits where the shirt and the tie are not the same color is \\(\\boxed{63}\\).",
